(footprint "DFB1550LP_Butterfly14_Mech"
	(version 20241229)
	(generator "gen_dfb_fp.py")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Thorlabs DFB1550LP 14-pin butterfly laser - MECHANICAL PLACEMENT AID, NO PADS. The package is held in an Azimuth 5253-100-7S + -7R ZIF socket pair and is never soldered, so it has no land pattern; this footprint is board_only and exists to position the two sockets, the heat spreader cutout and the fiber exit. GEOMETRY from Thorlabs DOC-102831 Rev A p.3 (drawing rasterised - the PDF text layer does not identify which dimension is which). AXES: rotated 90 deg CCW from the datasheet top view so the lead rows run along Y at 2.54 mm pitch, matching the Azimuth socket footprints exactly - place JZ1 (S) at -X and JZ2 (R) at +X, both at rotation 0, and lead-to-contact alignment in Y is automatic. Body 12.70 mm across the lead rows x 20.80 mm along the fiber axis; lead rows exit at X = +/-6.35; 7 leads per row at Y = +7.62 .. -7.62. PIN 1 and PIN 14 are both at the FIBER end (+Y): pins 1-7 run down the -X row from Y=+7.62, pins 8-14 run up the +X row to Y=+7.62. Mounting flanges carry 4x Ø2.7 mm holes at X=+/-4.45, Y=+/-13.0 (8.9 mm across x 26.0 mm along) - these are for screwing the package to a heat spreader, they are NOT PCB holes and are drawn on F.Fab/User.Drawings only. HEIGHTS (front view): body 7.3 mm tall, baseplate flange 1.0 mm thick, LEAD PLANE 4.0 mm above the baseplate bottom. The Azimuth contact plane is 7.62 mm above the PCB face, so the butterfly baseplate bottom lands 7.62 - 4.00 = 3.62 mm above the board - that is the gap the heat spreader must close. ACROSS THE LEAD ROWS the body is 12.70 mm and each lead extends 11.5/11.25 mm clear of it, giving a LEAD TIP-TO-TIP SPAN of 35.45 mm - measured 2026-08-05 from Thorlabs' own DFB1550LP-Step.step, which also gives 30.00 mm overall along the package incl. flanges, a 20.52 mm lid (the datasheet's 20.8), a 17.78 mm lead-row span (7 x 2.54) and 7.20 mm body height. NOTE 20.8 mm is the body ALONG the fiber axis, NOT across the leads - 7 leads at 2.54 span 17.78 mm and cannot fit a 12.70 mm edge, so the rows must be the 12.70 apart pair. SOCKET PITCH: with these leads the usable S-to-R pitch (body centre to centre, 12.70 mm sockets) runs 25.40 to 37.46 mm, bounded below by the package fouling the socket faces and above by the lead no longer reaching the odd-contact column 5.33 mm inboard of the datum edge. BTF_Card is laid out at 28.81 mm: 1.70 mm body-to-socket clearance, 9.67 mm of lead inside each socket, clearing the odd column by 4.34 mm and the even by 7.51 mm, both well past the Azimuth 3.81 mm minimum engagement. Flange outer edge at Y=+/-15.0 - not dimensioned. Fiber boot Ø5.8 exits +Y for 24.0 mm; respect the fiber bend radius beyond that. 3D MODEL: built by lib/extract_dfb_3d.py from Thorlabs' own DFB1550LP-Step.step via the cyclic permutation (Xs,Ys,Zs)->(Zs,Xs,Ys) (a proper rotation, so the part is NOT mirrored), seated with the baseplate bottom 3.62 mm above the board. The long fiber run is trimmed; the boot stub is kept.")
	(tags "thorlabs dfb1550lp butterfly 14-pin laser mechanical placement aid no-pads azimuth zif")
	(attr board_only exclude_from_pos_files exclude_from_bom)
